# Fluig Dev

Platform for generating, reviewing, correcting, validating, and documenting TOTVS Fluig datasets. Do not execute generated Fluig JavaScript.

## Stack and layout

- Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript, Node.js, Tailwind CSS 4, local JSON persistence (Supabase is not required for local single-user use), OpenAI API, Monaco Editor, Lucide React.
- `projects/customer/src/app`: pages and API routes.
- `projects/customer/src/components`: reusable UI.
- `projects/customer/src/lib`: shared utilities and constants.
- `projects/customer/src/server`: server-side business logic and integrations.
- `projects/customer/src/types`: shared types.
- `docs`: technical documentation.

## Development

- TypeScript only. Keep components small and reusable.
- Keep frontend logic out of `src/server`. Keep secrets and API keys on the server.
- Validate every API input. Handle errors explicitly; do not swallow them.
- User-facing UI text is Portuguese (Brazil). Keep the dark professional visual identity (navy, discreet purple).
- Do not present unimplemented integrations as connected or working.
- Review and test changes before treating them as complete.

## Fluig

- Do not invent Fluig APIs or methods. Use only APIs documented for the configured Fluig version, and state that version when generating code.
- Distinguish internal datasets, custom/advanced datasets, and integrations. Say which one the output is.
- Preserve the business rules the user provided. Explain dependencies and compatibility limits.
- If a requested method is not confirmed for the configured version, say so and stop. Do not substitute an invented call.

```javascript
// Bad: invented API
dataset.addRow(DatasetBuilder.create(values));

// Good: offline dataset structure documented by TOTVS; column names in uppercase
function defineStructure() {
  addColumn("CODIGO");
  addColumn("DESCRICAO");
  setKey(["CODIGO"]);
}
```
